---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="J3 Importaciones | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="j3importaciones" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/J3Impor.svg" alt="J3 Importaciones website preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">J3 Importaciones Brand and Website</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A brand identity and WordPress website built from scratch for an import business, using Elementor to move quickly from concept to a manageable live site.</p>
      <a href="https://j3importaciones.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View site <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>J3 Importaciones needed a complete digital foundation: brand identity, website structure, and a CMS setup that could be edited without a complex development workflow.</p>
      <p>The project followed a similar approach to Globalink: define the brand, organize the business message, and build a practical WordPress site that could support the next phase of the company.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Brand design, website planning, WordPress configuration, Elementor development, responsive layout, content organization, and deployment support.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>The business needed a visual identity and a website that felt established enough for customers and partners, while still being simple to maintain and fast to launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Created the brand foundation and translated it into a web interface.</li>
        <li>Defined the core page structure around business credibility, services, and contact flow.</li>
        <li>Built the website in WordPress with Elementor to balance speed and editor flexibility.</li>
        <li>Kept sections modular so the site could grow with more services, products, or landing pages.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>J3 Importaciones received a complete web presence that combines branding, content structure, and a usable CMS. It is a practical example of taking a business from zero digital identity to a live, editable website.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
